{"id": "EUVD-2026-86685", "enisaUuid": "f3009832-de56-3518-8e0e-cf3ea4bfe10a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing: Fix subbuf resize races with trace_pipe_raw readers\n\nConcurrent subbuffer resizes may crash trace_pipe_raw readers or leak\nuninitialized memory to userspace due to stale size values.\n\nModify ring_buffer_alloc_read_page() to handle the resizing of an\nexisting buffer_data_read_page if necessary and add a new\nring_buffer_read_page_size(). This new function enables ring-buffer\nbuffer_data_read_page users to not call the racy\nring_buffer_subbuf_size_get(). This makes the spare_size member of\nftrace_buffer_info redundant.\n\nFinally, handle buffer_data_read_page/reader_page order discrepancy in\nring_buffer_read_page(). On a mismatch simply copy manually the data to\nthe buffer_data_read_page.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:06", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/574efd988d116bd56ac688ab2d64e06ba0da982a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3f30b2cd4eba45c05f822f03f1b0f4077d6d4dc3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/75b37b8369778b69ce9738d1c97685a1615cb252", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dae8dda341d2d9034a90d59e8a7d502e1263813f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wpxh-73rr-fxf7", "CVE-2026-98032"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d554963-b7de-307d-9c0f-a6254b947eff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "2f109a3f-ca38-3095-99cf-6051372e9d42", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "41856ae7-5a14-39d1-8b51-1e4ea0dcd167", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bce761d757452ba5eb77e11fecc37a04b67494e7 <574efd988d116bd56ac688ab2d64e06ba0da982a"}, {"id": "4a0bdebe-4172-36f4-ab9d-cbb8e70cb800", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bce761d757452ba5eb77e11fecc37a04b67494e7 <3f30b2cd4eba45c05f822f03f1b0f4077d6d4dc3"}, {"id": "65535096-c840-3923-9242-33531e01ab46", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "9f73c75d-38c7-3903-ab12-c2effcf73c12", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "cc794b41-bd83-3471-99c1-d9c77675bd76", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bce761d757452ba5eb77e11fecc37a04b67494e7 <75b37b8369778b69ce9738d1c97685a1615cb252"}, {"id": "dac48a8a-5e07-351d-a5c5-e9c464807225", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f0783fb5-1692-3401-9b6f-4187d3750ac7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "fe902a97-cef5-398e-8396-9417bb6228eb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bce761d757452ba5eb77e11fecc37a04b67494e7 <dae8dda341d2d9034a90d59e8a7d502e1263813f"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6b0d0ccb-1f77-31ab-85b2-f91dfd302044", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}